{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1417425-lycian-antagonist-for-a-mage-game","id":1417425,"title":"Lycian antagonist for a Mage Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-09T02:58:50-07:00","id":1417425,"title":"Lycian antagonist for a Mage Game","content":"I thought to be creative and surprise my mage players by using a Quixotic Lycian as one of the major antagonists in the game. She would be the embodiment of one of the character's memories of a specific individual. Her thesis is to well manipulate and test mages so that they can become stronger. But as Changeling is one of the games I am less knowledgeable of, I would love some help in designing a Chimera that can be a threat to a cabal of mages <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Custom redes beyond those that exist in c20 and the c20 player's guide is also helpful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T05:35:59-07:00","id":1417432,"title":"","content":"Hm, maybe give her the Changeling ally merit, and give her a more powerful dupe. I also suggest given them the entrancement and illustration redes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 10-09-2020, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-09T12:27:35-08:00","id":1434976,"title":"","content":"I did something similar to this, but for a WtA game. No CtD-related words or phrases ever got brought in, but my players\u2019 pack dealt with a family of Thallain Kinain they were absolutely sure were a Black Spiral family of Kinfolk. Sense Wyrm never detected them (as Thallain are of the Wyld), so the pack was convinced <i>this</i> family had a fetish that cloaked it\u2019s taint.<br /> <br /> To this day I\u2019m not sure they\u2019ve figured it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T03:42:20-07:00","id":1461935,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Thats really nice! But i know some <a href=\"https://www.essayontime.co.uk/\" target=\"_blank\">essay writing service</a> that can do much more help for students. Just check their reviews, and if you will need any type of help with paper tasks. Just write to them!</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27000,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27000-adamsmith","user":"AdamSmith","date":". 10-11-2021, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27000-adamsmith","name":"AdamSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T19:29:01-07:00","id":1462063,"title":"","content":"One option is to give it something to kidnap the players to the Dreaming, and follow the rules for the Dreaming in C20. It isn't exactly like the rest of the Umbra and the realm may challenge their concepts of how their magic should behave there. No Sphere would be particularly more or less potent in the Dreaming, but they can have far different effects as Chimerae don't follow consistent rules when you define what kind of Pattern one of them would be (Is it Life or Matter? Does this thing have a Mind? Which ones count as Spirits? How can I defy the very concepts of Space and Time when I'm not even sure of what are those concepts around here?)<br /> <br /> My opinion about redes is that despite the small number of options relatively speaking, the best ones to build up upon are already on the core. Befuddle can wreck havoc, and is likely to completely nullify their Arete. Hide and Scuttle are very effective at what they do. And for a Chimera that deals with Mages I would adapt Steal Glamour into Steal Quintessence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}